<p>The man with the longest surname in Fiji is Levani Mavoaiuluivitimaitaveunienanodralakicakacakatakanavalenilotunagon<br />
enivadravadraenaesitetimaiuraqaicuruvularuaenavaleniveivakabulaimaiwaiyevoenayasanakocakaudrove.</p>
<p>It means &#8220;injured (mavoa) while on Taveuni when the people of Vadravadra went to work at Ura Estate where he got injured and was later admitted for two months at the Waiyevo Hospital in the province of Cakaudrove.&#8221; It was given to him deliberately to set the record.</p>
<p>He goes by Levani Mavoa. &#8220;I can remember my date of birth,&#8221; <a href="https://www.fijitimes.com.fj/whats-in-a-name-a-surname-with-160-letters/">he told the <em>Fiji Times</em></a>, &#8220;but I cannot remember my full name.&#8221;</p>
